Re: [PATCH] Re: [perl #46073] split function broken on MacOS On 2007–10–05, at 16:43, H.Merijn Brand wrote:

> You made it too ugly imho
>
> -    print join(':', split(/ */, 'hi there'));
> +    print(join(':', split(/ */, 'hi there')), "\\n");
> *    print join(':', split(/ */, 'hi there'), "\\n");

But that produces slightly different output:

$ perl
print join(':', split(/ */, 'hi there'), "\\n");
h:i:t:h:e:r:e:
$ perl
print(join(':', split(/ */, 'hi there')), "\\n");
h:i:t:h:e:r:e

